597     // When branch prediction is enabled a skid buffer between the IF and ID/EX stage is introduced.
598     // If an instruction in IF is predicted to be a taken branch and ID/EX is not ready the
599     // instruction in IF is moved to the skid buffer which becomes the output of the IF stage until
600     // the ID/EX stage accepts the instruction. The skid buffer is required as otherwise the ID/EX
601     // ready signal is coupled to the instr_req_o output which produces a feedthrough path from
602     // data_gnt_i -> instr_req_o (which needs to be avoided as for some interconnects this will
603     // result in a combinational loop).
