│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is a PMP/cosim mismatch for an instruction fetch that    │
│ straddles a PMP TOR boundary.                                      │
│ Spike correctly raises Instruction Access Fault at 0x80005cc4 (TOR │
│ end, exclusive).                                                   │
│ Ibex misses that fault in this scenario.                           │
│                                                                    │
│ This happens when a 32-bit instruction starts at a                 │
│ halfword-aligned but word-unaligned address (i.e., instruction     │
│ straddles two words / two PMP checks are needed).                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the bug is                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv, in PMP error combination       │
│ logic:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assign if_instr_pmp_err = pmp_err_if_i |                          │
│                            (if_instr_addr[2] & ~instr_is_compress  │
│  & pmp_err_if_plus2_i);                                            │
│  ...                                                               │
│  assign if_instr_err_plus2 = ((if_instr_addr[2] &                  │
│  ~instr_is_compressed & pmp_err_if_plus2_i) |                      │
│                               fetch_err_plus2) & ~pmp_err_if_i;    │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ For unaligned 32-bit instructions, the relevant indicator is       │
│ address bit [1] (halfword offset), not bit [2].                    │
│ Using bit [2] causes the second-half PMP check to be skipped for   │
│ cases like ...cc2 -> ...cc4, exactly the reported case.            │
│                                                                    │
