│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The pipeline flush logic for CSR writes in ibex_id_stage.sv only   │
│ flushes for PMP-related CSRs (mseccfg, pmpcfg*, pmpaddr*) when the │
│ CSR op is CSR_OP_WRITE or CSR_OP_SET.                              │
│ CSR_OP_CLEAR updates those CSRs too, but currently does not        │
│ trigger a flush.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ That can leave already-fetched instructions validated against      │
│ stale PMP settings, which is a correctness/security issue.         │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In rtl/ibex_id_stage.sv, block csr_pipeline_flushes:               │
│                                                                    │
│  • First branch (csr_op_o == CSR_OP_WRITE || csr_op_o ==           │
│    CSR_OP_SET) includes CSR_MSECCFG and PMP register address range │
│    check.                                                          │
│  • CSR_OP_CLEAR is excluded from this branch.                      │
│  • Second branch (csr_op_o != CSR_OP_READ) only handles debug      │
│    CSRs.                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ So PMP/ePMP clears are missed.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior changes minimal and targeted.                     │
│  • Preserve existing intended behavior for non-PMP CSRs (e.g.      │
│    mstatus, mie still flush only for write/set).                   │
│  • Ensure all PMP/ePMP mutations (WRITE/SET/CLEAR) trigger flush.  │
│  • Keep combinational logic simple and deterministic.              │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Refactor the condition so:                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • mstatus/mie: flush on WRITE/SET only (existing behavior         │
│    retained).                                                      │
│  • mseccfg, all PMP CSRs, and debug CSRs: flush on any modifying   │
│    CSR op (csr_op_o != CSR_OP_READ), which includes CSR_OP_CLEAR.  │
