│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The pipeline flush logic for CSR writes misses CSR_OP_CLEAR when   │
│ updating PMP-related CSRs (PMPCFGx, PMPADDRx, and MSECCFG).        │
│ As a result, after clearing PMP bits, already-fetched instructions │
│ may continue based on stale PMP permissions and execute when they  │
│ should be blocked.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In rtl/ibex_id_stage.sv, inside csr_pipeline_flushes:              │
│                                                                    │
│  • PMP/MSECCFG flushes are currently only triggered for:           │
│     • CSR_OP_WRITE                                                 │
│     • CSR_OP_SET                                                   │
│  • CSR_OP_CLEAR is excluded in that path.                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Specifically, this conditional is the root cause:                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (csr_op_en_o == 1'b1 && (csr_op_o == CSR_OP_WRITE || csr_op_o  │
│  == CSR_OP_SET)) begin                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ which gates the PMP/MSECCFG checks.                                │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior unchanged where intentional (e.g., mstatus/mie    │
│    clear can remain non-flushing).                                 │
│  • Ensure PMP/ePMP modifications flush for all modifying CSR ops   │
│    (WRITE, SET, CLEAR).                                            │
│  • Avoid regressions for debug CSR flush behavior.                 │
│  • Keep the patch minimal and localized.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Refactor the flush logic to:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • Flush for MSTATUS/MIE only on WRITE/SET (existing intent).      │
│  • Flush for MSECCFG and all PMP CSRs on any non-read op (includes │
│    CLEAR).                                                         │
│  • Keep debug CSR flushes on any non-read op.                      │
│  • Use independent if checks under csr_op_en_o, avoiding the       │
│    previous if/else if interaction.                                │
