│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The ID stage only triggers a CSR-related pipeline flush for        │
│ PMP/ePMP CSRs when the CSR op is CSR_OP_WRITE or CSR_OP_SET.       │
│ CSR_OP_CLEAR updates were unintentionally excluded, so clearing    │
│ PMP-related CSRs can leave already-fetched instructions validated  │
│ against stale PMP state.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ In rtl/ibex_id_stage.sv, inside csr_pipeline_flushes:              │
│                                                                    │
│  • First branch flushes for MSTATUS, MIE, MSECCFG, and PMP CSRs    │
│    only for WRITE/SET                                              │
│  • Second branch flushes debug CSRs for any non-READ op            │
│                                                                    │
│ So PMP/MSECCFG with CSR_OP_CLEAR falls through without flush.      │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep fix minimal and local to flush qualification logic.        │
│  • Preserve existing intentional behavior (e.g., MSTATUS/MIE flush │
│    only for operations that can newly expose IRQ handling          │
│    behavior).                                                      │
│  • Ensure all PMP/ePMP modifications (WRITE/SET/CLEAR) flush       │
│    pipeline.                                                       │
│  • Avoid broad behavior changes outside issue scope.               │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Update csr_pipeline_flushes so:                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • MSTATUS/MIE keep existing WRITE/SET flush condition.            │
│  • MSECCFG and PMP (instr_rdata_i[31:25] == 7'h1D) flush on any    │
│    non-READ CSR op (thus including CLEAR).                         │
│  • Debug CSR flush behavior remains unchanged (non-READ).          │
