I looked at where the “oh_raddr_a_err/b_err” and “oh_we_err” signals are declared in ibex_register_file_fpga.sv and saw that they only ever get driven inside the “if (RdataMuxCheck)” branch, so if RdataMuxCheck=0 they float. The fix is to give them a default (e.g. tie off to zero) outside that branch or in the else. The only file that needs changing is:

```  
rtl/ibex_register_file_fpga.sv  
```
