╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI probe interface expects PMP address CSR read values as    │
│ 32-bit words:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • csr_pmpaddr_q_i[PMP_MAX_REGIONS] is declared as logic [31:0].   │
│                                                                    │
│ But the connected internal signal in cv32e40s_cs_registers is      │
│ declared as:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • logic [PMP_ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] pmp_addr_rdata[PMP_MAX_REGIONS];     │
│                                                                    │
│ For configurations where PMP_ADDR_WIDTH != 32 (e.g. with           │
│ non-default granularity), this causes:                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • type mismatch at elaboration (Xcelium error),                   │
│  • and incorrect RVFI CSR value representation in formal flows.    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Primary issue is in:                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • rtl/cv32e40s_cs_registers.sv (declaration of pmp_addr_rdata)    │
│  • manifested at the wrapper connection in                         │
│    bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv:                                        │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )    │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep internal storage width optimized if needed (pmp_addr_q     │
│    etc.) but expose CSR read-data probe at architectural width     │
│    (32-bit for RV32 CSR visibility).                               │
│  • Minimize RTL impact: only adjust the RVFI-facing read-data      │
│    signal width.                                                   │
│  • Avoid changing testbench/tests; fix RTL typing at source.       │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Change pmp_addr_rdata declaration to 32-bit per entry:             │
│                                                                    │
│  • from logic [PMP_ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] ...                             │
│  • to   logic [31:0] ...                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ This resolves the wrapper/RVFI port type mismatch and ensures RVFI │
│ receives full-width CSR read values.                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
