│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The core is raising the wrong exception type for a misaligned load │
│ (lh) when ZICCLSM (misaligned load/store support) is not enabled.  │
│ In the failing case, the load address is both:                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • misaligned (should trigger exception code 4: Load Address       │
│    Misaligned), and                                                │
│  • in an invalid/forbidden region (can also trigger Load Access    │
│    Fault).                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ Wally is currently reporting Load Access Fault instead of Load     │
│ Address Misaligned.                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in src/mmu/mmu.sv, in how fault outputs are           │
│ generated:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • LoadMisalignedFaultM / StoreAmoMisalignedFaultM are computed    │
│    correctly.                                                      │
│  • But LoadAccessFaultM / StoreAmoAccessFaultM are also asserted   │
│    independently from PMA/PMP logic.                               │
│  • If trap logic prioritizes access fault (or both are high),      │
│    wrong cause can be observed.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Relevant lines in provided context:                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assign LoadAccessFaultM     = (PMALoadAccessFaultM ... ) &        │
│  ~TLBMiss;                                                         │
│  assign StoreAmoAccessFaultM = (PMAStoreAmoAccessFaultM ... ) &    │
│  ~TLBMiss;                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ These should be suppressed when misaligned fault is already active │
│ (except cases where misaligned is intentionally converted to       │
│ access fault, already handled by existing                          │
│ AtomicMisalignedCausesAccessFaultM logic).                         │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep change minimal and local to fault-generation point.        │
│  • Preserve existing atomic special-case behavior.                 │
│  • Avoid touching tests or unrelated modules.                      │
│  • Make exception signaling mutually consistent so only the        │
│    architecturally intended cause is seen.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Gate access faults with the corresponding misaligned fault         │
│ outputs:                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • LoadAccessFaultM should be deasserted when LoadMisalignedFaultM │
│    is asserted.                                                    │
│  • StoreAmoAccessFaultM should be deasserted when                  │
│    StoreAmoMisalignedFaultM is asserted.                           │
│                                                                    │
│ This enforces misaligned priority for non-ZICCLSM paths while      │
│ preserving existing behavior for supported misaligned handling and │
│ atomic corner cases.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 1                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
