│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The core is raising the wrong exception type when a load/store     │
│ address is both:                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • misaligned, and                                                 │
│  • also hits an access-fault condition (PMA/PMP).                  │
│                                                                    │
│ In the reported scenario (lh x5,0(x5) with x5 = 0xffffffff,        │
│ Zicclsm disabled), Wally reports Load Access Fault instead of Load │
│ Address Misaligned (exception code 4).                             │
│ For this project’s expected behavior (and the referenced Priv spec │
│ interpretation), misaligned should win here when misaligned        │
│ accesses are not supported in hardware.                            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
