│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The reported “Attempting to read from uninitialized RAM” warning   │
│ is a false positive during an MMIO load (GPIO register),           │
│ especially visible around WFI/interrupt activity.                  │
│                                                                    │
│ In this flow, the detector is checking load data too early (while  │
│ memory stage can still be stalled / data not yet valid), so        │
│ transient/unknown bus data is interpreted as an uninitialized RAM  │
│ read.                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In testbench/testbench.sv, the ramxdetector is instantiated with   │
│ raw read intent:                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  ramxdetector #(P.XLEN, P.LLEN) ramxdetector(clk,                  │
│  dut.core.lsu.MemRWM[1], ...);                                     │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ dut.core.lsu.MemRWM[1] alone is not sufficient to indicate “safe   │
│ to validate read data” in all cycles (notably MMIO and stalled     │
│ memory transactions).                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Only run X-data checks when a memory-stage instruction is       │
│    actually valid for checking.                                    │
│  • Gate debug checkers with pipeline-valid / non-stalled           │
│    conditions to avoid false alarms from transient bus values.     │
│  • Keep fix minimal and non-invasive (testbench-side only).        │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Qualify ramxdetector read-enable input with:                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • InstrValidM (instruction in M stage is valid), and              │
│  • ~StallM (stage is not stalled).                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ This prevents checking incomplete/unstable load data and removes   │
│ spurious uninitialized-RAM warnings for MMIO accesses.             │
