│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ without gating by stage validity/read completion                   │
│ (StallM/InstrValidM).                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ This can trigger duplicate/false warnings during wait states       │
│ (which matches the log showing repeated warnings before the actual │
│ valid MEMR print).                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • Only run X-detection checks when data is architecturally        │
│    meaningful (valid instruction, non-stalled stage).              │
│  • Avoid checking transient bus values during multi-cycle MMIO     │
│    access.                                                         │
