│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The reported behavior has two symptoms during WFI + interrupt      │
│ activity:                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • False warnings:                                                 │
│    Attempting to read from uninitialized RAM appears even for a    │
│    valid MMIO load (GPIO_OUTPUT_VAL at 0x1006000c).                │
│  • Confusing interrupt timing in logs (mip.MTIP rises/falls around │
│    WFI), which looks inconsistent with instruction-level trace     │
│    points.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The first symptom is a real tracer/testbench issue. The second is  │
│ largely a trace correlation artifact (net-change events vs         │
│ retired-instruction logs), but the false RAM-X warnings make this  │
│ much harder to interpret.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the issue occurs                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ In testbench/testbench.sv, ramxdetector is instantiated with a raw │
│ memory-read qualifier:                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  ramxdetector #(P.XLEN, P.LLEN) ramxdetector(clk,                  │
│  dut.core.lsu.MemRWM[1], ...                                       │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This can fire during pipeline hold/stall windows (including around │
│ WFI), where ReadDataM may be transient/unknown before a completed  │
│ valid read. That creates false “uninitialized RAM” warnings.       │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Gate debug detectors with pipeline validity and non-stalled     │
│    stage conditions.                                               │
│  • Keep fix minimal and localized to testbench tracing logic.      │
│  • Avoid touching architectural behavior or uncore logic for a     │
│    tracing-only symptom.                                           │
│  • Preserve existing detector semantics for truly valid M-stage    │
│    reads.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Add a gated read-enable signal for ramxdetector:                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • require MemRWM[1]                                               │
│  • require InstrValidM                                             │
│  • require ~StallM                                                 │
│                                                                    │
