╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ From the issue log, there are two observed anomalies during a      │
│ WFI/interrupt loop:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • False warning: Attempting to read from uninitialized RAM when   │
│    reading GPIO MMIO (0x1006000c), which is not RAM.               │
│  • Confusing interrupt timing (mip.MTIP rise/fall appears          │
│    misaligned with instruction trace context).                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The first one is clearly a tracer/testbench instrumentation issue  │
│ (RAM-X detector is being applied to MMIO reads).                   │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the problem occurs                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ In testbench/testbench.sv, the ramxdetector is currently driven    │
│ directly by all load operations:                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  ramxdetector #(P.XLEN, P.LLEN) ramxdetector(clk,                  │
│  dut.core.lsu.MemRWM[1], ...)                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This means it also checks MMIO reads (like GPIO), which can        │
│ legitimately return values without being tracked as initialized    │
│ RAM in the RAM model.                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep checker scope precise: RAM uninitialized-read checker      │
│    should only monitor actual RAM accesses, not MMIO.              │
│  • Gate checkers with instruction validity to avoid warning on     │
│    bubbles/transient pipeline states.                              │
│  • Make minimal change in testbench instrumentation only (no DUT   │
│    functional change).                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Add a small gating signal before ramxdetector:                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Require a valid memory read instruction (MemRWM[1] +            │
│    InstrValidM)                                                    │
│  • Restrict detector to RAM-like address space (here, 0x8...       │
│    region), excluding MMIO (0x1..., 0x2... etc.)                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Then pass that gated signal into ramxdetector.                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
