│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs sometimes fails for specific seeds because the    │
│ randomized direct register loads (toggle_load) can start too early │
│ and overwrite register contents during the initial directed sanity │
│ check (write then immediate read of address 0x0).                  │
│                                                                    │
│ That makes the expected value DEADBEEF nondeterministic, causing   │
│ failures like:                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • observed data: de01beef                                         │
│  • expected data: deadbeef                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the directed write/read      │
│    check first.                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts immediately and spawns         │
│    toggle_load for all bytes right after reset.                    │
│  • toggle_load randomly asserts reg_load[byte_i], potentially      │
│    modifying bytes of the same register being checked.             │
│                                                                    │
│ So there is a race/collision between:                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • directed AXI read expectation                                   │
│  • asynchronous/random direct byte loads                           │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the deterministic “known-value” check isolated from random │
│    background activity.                                            │
│  • Start random stimulus only after directed checks complete.      │
│  • Minimize testbench behavior changes so random stress still runs │
│    as intended afterward.                                          │
│  • Avoid broad refactoring; use a clear synchronization point.     │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce an event to gate start of proc_generate_direct_load:     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Declare a synchronization event.                                │
│  • Trigger it only after the directed write/read assertions pass.  │
│  • Make proc_generate_direct_load wait on this event before        │
│    spawning toggle_load tasks.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves existing random behavior during                     │
│ lite_axi_master.run(...), while preventing collisions with the     │
│ initial expected-response check.                                   │
│                                                                    │
