│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem statement                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure is a testbench race/interference issue: in             │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs, the per-byte random direct load generator        │
│ (toggle_load) can modify register contents while the directed      │
│ “write then immediate readback” sanity check is running.           │
│ With some seeds, reg_load updates byte lanes between the directed  │
│ write and read, so read data becomes e.g. de01beef instead of full │
│ DEADBEEF, triggering the assertion.                                │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs deterministic write/read     │
│    check first.                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load() for all bytes    │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load() begins random load activity right away after      │
│    reset.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ So the deterministic check and random direct-load traffic overlap. │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic sanity checks isolated from                  │
│    random/background stimulus.                                     │
│  • Start stress/random stimulus only after baseline directed       │
│    checks pass.                                                    │
│  • Make minimal TB changes; do not alter DUT behavior for a TB     │
│    scheduling issue.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a start gate signal for random direct loads:             │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add start_rand_load signal.                                     │
│  • Initialize it to 0 in AXI traffic process.                      │
│  • Set it to 1 only after the directed write/read check completes  │
│    (just before lite_axi_master.run(...)).                         │
│  • In toggle_load, wait for start_rand_load before entering the    │
│    random forever loop.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes seed-dependent collision while preserving random      │
│ testing afterward.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
