│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure is caused by a race between:                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • the directed sanity check (write DEADBEEF... then read it back  │
│    at address 0), and                                              │
│  • the random direct register load generator (toggle_load) that    │
│    can asynchronously overwrite bytes in reg_q.                    │
│                                                                    │
│ For some seeds, random reg_load updates happen before/around that  │
│ directed read, so the readback data is no longer DEADBEEF, causing │
│ the assertion failure.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the directed write/read      │
│    check first.                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load() for all bytes    │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load() can assert reg_load[byte_i] with random timing,   │
│    including during the directed check window.                     │
│                                                                    │
│ So the directed expectation is not isolated from random            │
│ perturbations.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed smoke checks deterministic.                       │
│  • Start random stress only after deterministic checks complete.   │
│  • Avoid changing functional behavior broadly; use minimal         │
│    synchronization/gating.                                         │
│  • Keep reset-time defaults explicit (e.g., random load disabled   │
│    until enabled).                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a small start gate (e.g., start_rand_load) that:         │
│                                                                    │
│  • is 0 at reset/start of simulation,                              │
│  • is set to 1 only after the directed write/read check is         │
│    finished,                                                       │
│  • is waited on by each toggle_load task before entering random    │
│    load loop.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves current random test behavior while removing         │
│ seed-dependent collision with the initial directed assertion.      │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
