│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure is caused by a race in tb_axi_lite_regs: the per-byte  │
│ random direct-load traffic (toggle_load) can start modifying       │
│ registers before the directed “write known value then read it      │
│ back” check completes.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ So in some seeds, between:                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • write 0xDEADBEEF to address 0                                   │
│  • read address 0                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ one or more bytes are asynchronously overwritten by random load,   │
│ producing data like de01beef and causing:                          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assert (data == axi_data_t'(64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF))                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ to fail.                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs deterministic write/read     │
│    sanity check.                                                   │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load spawns toggle_load tasks immediately  │
│    after reset.                                                    │
│  • toggle_load begins random updates as soon as reset is           │
│    deasserted.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ These two flows are concurrent and unsynchronized during the       │
│ directed sanity phase.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic sanity checks isolated from random           │
│    background stimulus.                                            │
│  • Introduce explicit phase synchronization between directed and   │
│    random traffic.                                                 │
│  • Make minimal changes and preserve existing random behavior for  │
│    the rest of the test.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Add a simple start gate for random direct-load activity:           │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add start_rand_load signal.                                     │
│  • Keep it 0 initially.                                            │
│  • Set it to 1 only after the directed read-back assertions.       │
│  • In toggle_load, wait for start_rand_load before entering random │
│    load loop.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ This prevents collisions in the deterministic check while keeping  │
│ random load behavior unchanged afterward.                          │
│                                                                    │
