│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure is seed-dependent because the testbench launches       │
│ random direct register loads (toggle_load) in parallel with the    │
│ initial directed AXI-Lite write/read sanity check at address 0x0.  │
│                                                                    │
│ So sometimes:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • directed write stores DEADBEEF,                                 │
│  • then random reg_load overwrites bytes before the directed read, │
│  • directed read returns unexpected data (e.g. de01beef), causing  │
│    assertion failure.                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs directed write/read first.   │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts immediately and spawns         │
│    toggle_load tasks for all bytes.                                │
│  • toggle_load begins random reg_load activity right after reset.  │
│                                                                    │
│ These concurrent processes race with the directed check.           │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed sanity checks isolated from random stress         │
│    traffic.                                                        │
│  • Add explicit synchronization between independent initial        │
│    blocks.                                                         │
│  • Prefer minimal intrusion: don’t alter DUT behavior, only        │
│    testbench scheduling.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a simple enable signal for random direct loads:          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Initialize it low.                                              │
│  • Set it high only after the directed write/read assertions       │
│    complete.                                                       │
│  • Make each toggle_load task wait for this enable before entering │
│    its random loop.                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes the seed-dependent collision while preserving         │
│ existing random-load behavior for the rest of simulation.          │
