│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a seed-dependent failure because the          │
│ background random direct-load traffic (toggle_load) can update     │
│ register bytes while the directed sanity check (write/read at      │
│ address 0x0) is still running.                                     │
│ So sometimes the readback is no longer DEADBEEF, causing this      │
│ assertion failure.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • Directed check is in proc_generate_axi_traffic (write/read +    │
│    strict data assert).                                            │
│  • Concurrent random register load generation starts independently │
│    in proc_generate_direct_load / toggle_load immediately after    │
│    reset.                                                          │
│  • Since both target same register bank, random load can overwrite │
│    bytes before the directed read completes.                       │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed deterministic checks isolated from random         │
│    background stimuli.                                             │
│  • Avoid race-prone concurrent drivers during known-value          │
│    assertions.                                                     │
│  • Make minimal testbench scheduling changes without altering DUT  │
│    behavior or test intent.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a simple enable gate for random direct-load activity:    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add a control signal (e.g. rand_load_en).                       │
│  • Keep it disabled during initial directed write/read check.      │
│  • Enable it only after that directed check passes.                │
│  • In toggle_load, wait for this enable before entering random     │
│    toggling loop.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps early deterministic checks stable while preserving      │
│ random stress phase behavior.                                      │
│                                                                    │
