│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem statement                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure in tb_axi_lite_regs is a race/flakiness issue: the     │
│ background random direct-load generator (toggle_load) can update   │
│ register bytes while the test is performing its initial            │
│ deterministic “write then read-back” check at address 0x0.         │
│                                                                    │
│ So in some seeds, one or more bytes are overwritten between the    │
│ write and read, producing values like de01beef instead of          │
│ deadbeef, which triggers the assertion.                            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs an early deterministic       │
│    write/read check.                                               │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load() threads          │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load() continuously asserts reg_load[byte_i] with random │
│    timing ($urandom_range), potentially targeting the same bytes   │
│    being validated.                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ These two flows are concurrent with no gating, causing             │
│ seed-dependent collisions.                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic sanity checks isolated from                  │
│    random/background disturbance.                                  │
│  • Gate randomized stimulus until after deterministic checks       │
│    complete.                                                       │
│  • Make minimal behavioral changes (don’t alter DUT protocol       │
│    behavior, only testbench sequencing).                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a small enable flag (e.g., start_rand_load) to delay     │
│ toggle_load() activity until the initial directed write/read       │
│ assertions pass.                                                   │
│ Sequence:                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Initialize start_rand_load = 0.                                 │
│  • Run deterministic write/read check.                             │
│  • Set start_rand_load = 1.                                        │
│  • Then run random AXI traffic and random direct loads             │
│    concurrently.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes the collision and makes the test deterministic across │
│ seeds.                                                             │
│                                                                    │
