│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a seed-dependent failure because the          │
│ background random direct-load traffic (toggle_load) can start too  │
│ early and modify register bytes while the test is still doing its  │
│ deterministic “write known value, then read it back” check.        │
│                                                                    │
│ So, in some seeds, the expected DEADBEEF... value is partially     │
│ overwritten before the read, producing mismatches like de01beef.   │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • The deterministic check is in proc_generate_axi_traffic         │
│    (write/read at address 0x0).                                    │
│  • Independent random register load generation starts in           │
│    proc_generate_direct_load, which immediately spawns toggle_load │
│    for all bytes after reset.                                      │
│  • toggle_load uses randomized delay and can hit register 0 bytes  │
│    before/around the deterministic read.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best-practice considerations                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed checks deterministic and isolated from random     │
│    background stimulus.                                            │
│  • Explicitly sequence concurrent TB processes with a              │
│    synchronization signal/event.                                   │
│  • Make minimal changes that do not alter DUT behavior, only       │
│    testbench race ordering.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a simple synchronization flag (e.g. start_rand_load) so  │
│ that:                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • deterministic write/read check runs first,                      │
│  • only after that, random direct-load generators are started.     │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves random stress during lite_axi_master.run(...) while │
│ removing seed-dependent collision during the directed sanity       │
│ check.                                                             │
