│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a seed-dependent failure in the directed      │
│ sanity check:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • test writes DEADBEEF... to address 0                            │
│  • then reads it back and expects exact match                      │
│  • sometimes read data is modified (e.g. de01beef) due to          │
│    concurrent random direct loads (reg_load / reg_d) started       │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ So the deterministic check is racing with random stimulus.         │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the directed write/read      │
│    check right after reset.                                        │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load spawns toggle_load() for every byte.  │
│  • toggle_load() starts random byte loads as soon as reset is      │
│    released (@(posedge rst_n)), which can overwrite bytes          │
│    before/during the directed readback.                            │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic smoke checks isolated from random background │
│    stimulus.                                                       │
│  • Avoid seed-dependent races in directed assertions.              │
│  • Make the minimal change: gate random-load generation until      │
│    after the directed check is complete.                           │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a small enable flag for random loads:                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • initialize it to 0                                              │
│  • set it to 1 only after directed write/read assertions are done  │
│  • in toggle_load(), wait for this enable before entering random   │
│    load loop.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves all existing random testing, but prevents           │
│ corruption of the initial deterministic readback.                  │
│                                                                    │
