│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a seed-dependent race: the background random  │
│ direct-load generator (toggle_load) can update reg_q while the     │
│ directed sanity check is trying to verify the first AXI write/read │
│ at address 0x0.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ So sometimes this sequence:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • AXI write DEADBEEF to 0x0                                       │
│  • AXI read from 0x0                                               │
│  • assert read data == DEADBEEF                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ fails because reg_load/reg_d changed those bytes in between.       │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the directed write/read and  │
│    expects deterministic data.                                     │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load spawns toggle_load for every byte     │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load can randomly start with rand_wait = 0, causing      │
│    immediate register overwrite before directed read assertion.    │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic smoke checks isolated from random background │
│    stimulus.                                                       │
│  • Avoid changing DUT semantics for a testbench scheduling         │
│    problem.                                                        │
│  • Use a simple explicit synchronization signal so random load     │
│    starts only after deterministic check passes.                   │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Add a start_rand_load control signal:                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • initialize it to 0 in proc_generate_axi_traffic,                │
│  • set it to 1 only after the directed read/check block,           │
│  • in toggle_load, wait for start_rand_load before entering random │
│    overwrite loop.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps the directed check stable while preserving existing     │
│ random stress behavior afterward.                                  │
