│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure is caused by a race/collision in the testbench: the    │
│ background direct-load randomizer (toggle_load) can modify         │
│ register bytes while the directed AXI write/read sanity check is   │
│ running.                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ So in some seeds, the sequence:                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • AXI write DEADBEEF to addr 0x0                                  │
│  • AXI read back from addr 0x0                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ is interrupted by a random reg_load update on one of those bytes,  │
│ producing values like DE01BEEF instead of DEADBEEF.                │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the directed write/read      │
│    check.                                                          │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load() for all bytes    │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load() continuously asserts reg_load[byte_i] with random │
│    values after reset.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ These run concurrently, so the directed check is                   │
│ non-deterministic.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed sanity checks deterministic.                      │
│  • Avoid concurrent randomized stimulus during known-value         │
│    assertions.                                                     │
│  • Synchronize background traffic with explicit start conditions   │
│    (gating signal/event), instead of relying on seed luck.         │
│  • Make minimal changes and preserve existing random coverage      │
│    afterward.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a start gate (e.g., start_rand_load) for toggle_load()   │
│ tasks:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • Initialize it to 0.                                             │
│  • In toggle_load(), wait(start_rand_load); before entering random │
│    load loop.                                                      │
│  • Set start_rand_load <= 1'b1; only after the directed readback   │
│    check passes, right before lite_axi_master.run(...).            │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps the initial write/read deterministic while preserving   │
│ random load behavior during the random test phase.                 │
│                                                                    │
