After digging into the original `clk_div.sv`, it becomes clear that its one‐shot counter never resets, so once it hits `RATIO–1` it toggles the clock once and then sits there.  To fix this, we must:

1. Provide a fully working integer divider in `clk_int_div.sv` (resetting the counter every half‐period to guarantee 50% duty).  
2. Deprecate or remove the broken logic in `clk_div.sv` (or at least stub it out).  
3. Update/extend the existing testbench (in `tb/clk_int_div_tb.sv`) to cover the new divider’s behavior.  
4. Add the new RTL file into the build (e.g. `CMakeLists.txt`).

Recommended files to edit, in priority order:

```  
src/rtl/clk_int_div.sv
src/rtl/clk_div.sv
tb/clk_int_div_tb.sv
CMakeLists.txt
```
