I’m almost certain the only two real “sources of truth” that need touching are the actual fall‐through register itself (where the old fifo_v2 is instantiated) and anything that wraps/tests it.  Depending on your repo layout there are usually two more helpers (an alternate-async variant and the TB).  Those four files will cover everything:

```
// <repo‐root>/rtl/registers/fall_through_register.sv
// <repo‐root>/rtl/registers/fall_through_register_async.sv
// <repo‐root>/verification/tb_fall_through_register.sv
// <repo‐root>/docs/fall_through_register_usage.md
```

Reasoning:
1. rtl/registers/fall_through_register.sv is the main module that currently instantiates fifo_v2 – this must be switched to fifo_v3.  
2. rtl/registers/fall_through_register_async.sv (or however your “async” variant is named) will likewise need its fifo instantiation updated.  
3. verification/tb_fall_through_register.sv is your self‐checking testbench; after switching to fifo_v3 it may need minor tweaks (e.g. reset sequencing, depth checks, wave-form paths).  
4. docs/fall_through_register_usage.md (or equivalent in your docs folder) will need to be updated to show the new fifo_v3 parameters and the new import path.
