I’ve identified that adding a “valid” flag to the shift‐register will require touching the RTL itself, the cell‐registry (so the new version shows up in the library), any tests that exercise shift_reg, and the user‐facing documentation. Based on the skeletons you provided, the four files most likely to require edits are:

```
rtl/shift_reg.sv
hdlspec/cells.json
tb/shift_reg_tb.sv
docs/common_cells.md
```

Reasoning:

1. rtl/shift_reg.sv – This is the shift‐register implementation; you need to add the “valid” input and the associated logic for the ICG insertion into the datapath.
2. hdlspec/cells.json – This JSON file lists all cells in the library; you must register your new/better shift_reg version so it’s discoverable by name and parameters.
3. tb/shift_reg_tb.sv – The existing testbench drives shift_reg; you’ll need to extend it to drive and check the new “valid” flag behavior.
