│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that dmi_jtag_tap.sv generates trst_no using logic    │
│ that is not safely synchronized. The current implementation        │
│ attempts to synthesize a reset by cycling through the JTAG         │
│ TestLogicReset state, but the resulting trst_no signal can glitch. │
│                                                                    │
│ That is dangerous because trst_no is used as an asynchronous reset │
│ in:                                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • dmi_jtag.sv                                                     │
│  • dmi_cdc.sv                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ A glitchy asynchronous reset can cause unintended resets,          │
│ metastability, or corrupted state.                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic code is in:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/dmi_jtag_tap.sv                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ Specifically, the logic around:                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • trst_sync1, trst_sync2                                          │
│  • the always_ff block that drives trst_no                         │
│  • the always_comb block that assigns trst_sync1 = trst_ni and     │
│    overrides it in TestLogicReset                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ The current structure mixes combinational and sequential           │
│ assignment in a way that can create unstable behavior for trst_no. │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Do not generate asynchronous reset signals from combinational   │
│    logic that can glitch.                                          │
│  • If a reset must be derived from a clocked domain, register it   │
│    cleanly and only change it on a clock edge.                     │
│  • Avoid assigning the same signal from both combinational and     │
│    sequential processes.                                           │
│  • Keep reset generation monotonic and synchronized.               │
│  • Prefer simple, explicit sequential logic for derived reset      │
│    signals.                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix should make trst_no a properly registered signal, updated  │
│ only in the tck_i clock domain, without combinational feedback.    │
│                                                                    │
│ A minimal safe solution is:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • remove the unsafe combinational assignment to trst_sync1 in     │
│    always_comb                                                     │
│  • initialize the synchronization chain safely on trst_ni          │
│    assertion                                                       │
│  • compute trst_no only from registered values                     │
│  • ensure trst_no is driven deterministically and does not glitch  │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves the intended functionality—resetting via JTAG       │
│ TestLogicReset—while avoiding a glitch-prone asynchronous reset    │
│ output.                                                            │
