│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is an off-by-one bug in the loop bound used to iterate   │
│ over halted_reshaped0 in src/dm_csrs.sv.                           │
│                                                                    │
│ halted_reshaped0 is declared as:                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  logic [(NrHarts-1)/2**5:0][31:0] halted_reshaped0;                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This means its valid indices go from 0 to (NrHarts-1)/2**5         │
│ inclusive.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ However, the loop currently uses:                                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  for (int unsigned k = 0; k < NrHarts/2**5+1; k++) begin           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ For some values of NrHarts, this upper bound is too large and can  │
│ cause the loop to access a non-existent array element.             │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic code is in src/dm_csrs.sv, in the p_reduction1     │
│ block around the haltsum1 reduction:                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  for (int unsigned k = 0; k < NrHarts/2**5+1; k++) begin           │
│    halted_flat1[k] = |halted_reshaped0[k];                         │
│  end                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is specifically in the loop bound compared to the          │
│ declaration of halted_reshaped0.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Loop bounds must match the declared array range exactly.        │
│  • Use expressions derived from the array declaration when         │
│    iterating over packed/unpacked dimensions.                      │
│  • Prefer inclusive-range-safe bounds for SystemVerilog arrays     │
│    declared as [high:0].                                           │
│  • Make minimal changes to avoid introducing unintended behavior   │
│    elsewhere.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Change the loop upper bound so it matches the actual number of     │
│ valid entries in halted_reshaped0, i.e.:                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  for (int unsigned k = 0; k < (NrHarts-1)/2**5+1; k++) begin       │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures the loop only accesses valid indices.                 │
