╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The SPI host FSM mishandles commands when the requested CSID       │
│ changes from the previous command. Instead of transitioning into   │
│ the CSB-switching path, it goes to WaitIdle, which causes the      │
│ first command after a CSID change to be skipped or delayed         │
│ incorrectly.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in:                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • hw/vendor/lowrisc_opentitan/spi_host/rtl/spi_host_fsm.sv        │
│                                                                    │
│ Specifically in the WaitIdle state logic, where the FSM decides    │
│ what to do after CSB is high and the idle delay has elapsed:       │
│                                                                    │
│  • if a new command is present and switch_required is true, the    │
│    FSM should go to CSBSwitch                                      │
│  • but the buggy behavior routes this case incorrectly in the      │
│    original implementation                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant decision point is the WaitIdle branch around the      │
│ switch_required check.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                   3. Best practices to consider                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Make the smallest possible change that fixes the FSM transition │
│    bug.                                                            │
│  • Preserve the intended state-machine structure and timing        │
│    behavior.                                                       │
│  • Ensure the fix matches the existing FSM design pattern used for │
│    CSB switching and idle delays.                                  │
│  • Avoid changing unrelated command parsing or register interface  │
│    logic.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                          4. How to fix it                          │
│                                                                    │
│ In the WaitIdle state, when idle_cntr_q == 4'h0 and a new command  │
│ is valid with a different CSID, the FSM should transition to       │
│ CSBSwitch instead of WaitIdle.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ This restores the correct sequence for CSID changes and ensures    │
│ the first command after a CSID switch is not skipped.              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]hw/vendor/lowrisc_opentitan/spi_host/rtl/spi_host_fsm.sv[/  │
│  le]                                                               │
│  [original]                                                        │
│            if (idle_cntr_q == 4'h0) begin                          │
│              prestall_st_d = WaitLead;                             │
│            end else begin                                          │
│              prestall_st_d = WaitIdle;                             │
│            end                                                     │
│  [/original]                                                       │
│  [patched]                                                         │
│            if (idle_cntr_q == 4'h0) begin                          │
│              prestall_st_d = WaitLead;                             │
│            end else begin                                          │
│              prestall_st_d = CSBSwitch;                            │
│            end                                                     │
│  [/patched]                                                        │
│                                                                    │
